From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neogram Patchset <patches@neogram.invalid>
Subject: misc/signature-check: native APK signature check for direct release builds

TMessagesProj/jni/CMakeLists.txt includes fork/jni/colorado/colorado.cmake when the build
passes NEO_COLORADO, which fork/gradle/neo-library.gradle does only for release builds that
have a release keystore, together with the CRC-32 and size of the keystore certificate and
the application id. The sources are compiled into libtmessages itself so the JNI entry point
NeoSignature.nativeVerify is always linked (exported through the Java_* rule of exports.map).
The Java side runs it after the first activity loaded the native library, only in direct
builds (Google Play re-signs Play builds), and only a certificate that was read and differs
stops the app.
---
 TMessagesProj/jni/CMakeLists.txt | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/TMessagesProj/jni/CMakeLists.txt b/TMessagesProj/jni/CMakeLists.txt
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/TMessagesProj/jni/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/TMessagesProj/jni/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -327,6 +327,11 @@ target_link_libraries(${NATIVE_LIB}
         cpufeatures
         breakpad)
 
+# Neogram APK signature check: release builds with a release keystore (fork/gradle/neo-library.gradle)
+if (NEO_COLORADO)
+    include(${NEO_COLORADO})
+endif ()
+
 #if (${ANDROID_ABI} STREQUAL "x86" OR ${ANDROID_ABI} STREQUAL "x86_64")
 #    target_link_libraries(${NATIVE_LIB}
 #            -Wl,--whole-archive vpxasm -Wl,--no-whole-archive
